## 4. Weighted Pugh Decision Matrix (I2: Trade-Off Analysis)

<!-- Baseline: Current system state (0). Scale: +1 (superior), 0 (neutral), -1 (inferior).
     Selection rule: Selected option must achieve Total Weighted Score > 0. -->
<pugh_matrix>

| Evaluation Dimension | Weight ($W_i$) | Baseline (Current) | Option A (Minimalist) | Option B (Idiomatic) | Option C (Extensible) |
|---|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| **1. Algorithm Complexity & I/O Latency** | **3** | 0 | | | |
| **2. Logic Isolation & Testability** | **3** | 0 | | | |
| **3. Backward API Compatibility** | **2** | 0 | | | |
| **4. Horizontal Scalability** | **2** | 0 | | | |
| **5. Technical Debt & Code Complexity** | **2** | 0 | | | |
| **Total Weighted Score ($\sum W_i \times S_{ij}$)** | -- | **0** | | | |

</pugh_matrix>

